  "notes": "USAGE:\nUsed both as a noun and as a suru-verb ({束縛|そくばく}する). Very common in discussions about relationships, where a controlling partner is described as {束縛|そくばく}が{強|つよ}い.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {束縛|そくばく}する (to restrain, to control)\n- {束縛|そくばく}から{逃|のが}れる (to escape from restraints)\n- {束縛|そくばく}が{強|つよ}い (to be very controlling)\n- {束縛|そくばく}を{受|う}ける (to be subjected to restrictions)",
